values ('ap_physics_c_mechanics', 2, '2.2', array['2.2', '2.3', '2.4', '2.5']::text[], 'diagram', 'Free-body diagram', 'A diagram of a single object or system showing every force exerted on it by the environment.', '[{"label": "Dot", "meaning": "Represents the center of mass; all force vectors originate here"}, {"label": "Force arrows", "meaning": "Each force exerted by the environment is drawn as its own straight arrow pointing in the direction of the force"}, {"label": "Same-direction forces", "meaning": "Drawn side by side, not overlapping"}, {"label": "Coordinate axis", "meaning": "One axis chosen parallel to the direction of acceleration (e.g., along an incline)"}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'On the AP exam draw individual forces only, not force components, on the free-body diagram.', 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-physics-c-mechanics-reference-u1-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_physics_c_mechanics-u2-r1-009; ced=2.2.B.2-2.2.B.4 and Boundary Statement "individual forces ... must be drawn side by side, not overlapping"')
