values ('ap_physics_c_mechanics', 2, '2.3', array['2.3', '2.10']::text[], 'vocabulary', 'Tension', 'Tension is the macroscopic net result of the forces that infinitesimal segments of a string, cable, chain, or similar system exert on each other in response to an external force.', '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Tension is uniform only for an ideal string (negligible mass, does not stretch). In a string with nonnegligible mass, tension may differ from point to point.', 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-physics-c-mechanics-reference-u1-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_physics_c_mechanics-u2-r2-001; ced=2.3.A.3: "Tension is the macroscopic net result of forces that infinitesimal segments of a string, cable, chain, or similar system exert on each other in response to an external force."')
